al 10 Development","noes":39,"question":"The majority of senators voted against [Lee Rhiannon's](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/lee_rhiannon) motion: > That the Senate: > > (a) notes that: > > * (i) the current [member for Warringah](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/warringah/tony_abbott) stated in 1997, in reference to development on Middle Head in Sydney Harbour, that he had organised a number of protest meetings and campaigned strongly to ensure this piece of heritage was not lost to the people of Sydney and Australia; > > * (ii) Liberal branches in the Warringah electorate have expressed concerns about the proposed development, including the Mosman Liberal Branch that passed a motion calling on the government to reject the development and instead work with the community towards a truly adaptive use of the present buildings; > > * (iii) a report on fire risk on Middle Head prepared by a former Australian Capital Territory chief fire control officer, Mr Roger Fenwick, noted that the current development proposal does not meet New South Wales fire protection standards for aged care facilities; and > > (b) calls on the Minister for the Environment, [Mr Hunt](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/flinders/greg_hunt), to reverse his approval for the proposed development application, and to not accept any new or amended application for development on the 10 Terminal site at Middle Head.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3632","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2014-12-02/3"}
